# Skip-list for esolang integration tests (TestEsolangPrograms). Format:
#
#   <phase> <lang>/<fixture>[: reason]
#
# - <phase>:
#     esolang        -- skip the fixture entirely (no assertion either way)
#     esolang-xfail  -- run the fixture; treat eval-error or stdout mismatch
#                       as expected. If the fixture actually passes, the
#                       harness emits t.Errorf so closed gaps surface as
#                       failures and the entry can be dropped.
# - path is "<lang>/<fixture-name-without-.in>"
# - lines starting with # and blank lines ignored
#
# When a goruby gap closes for an xfail entry: drop the line; the fixture
# then becomes plain regression coverage. When a gap regresses for a plain
# entry: add an xfail line w/ the failing reason rather than deleting the
# fixture.

# --- newly vendored interpreters (5/2026) -----------------------------
# These were added alongside the wiki's "16 langs with ruby refs" survey.
# Marked xfail until we know whether the current evaluator handles them
# end-to-end; first test run will flip the ones already passing into
# unexpected-pass failures and we can drop those entries.

esolang-xfail mariolang/output4: newly vendored; goruby support unverified
esolang-xfail rasel/helloworld: newly vendored; goruby support unverified
esolang-xfail ropy/hello_world: newly vendored; goruby support unverified
